# Implementation Plan: Document Photo Extraction & Circular Magnifier

This plan outlines adding the new **"Document Photo"** section to the PehchaanAI Verification Result page, integrating server-side face crop detection with quality evaluation, and implementing a smooth circular magnifying-glass inspection lens on the frontend.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Zero breaking changes**: Existing modules (MRZ cross-checks, Verhoeff crypto checks, Tampering/ELA detection, Biometric webcam match, Blockchain record anchoring) remain completely untouched and working.
> - **Strict Real Data**: No hardcoded/mocked photos will be used. The photo is strictly cropped from the uploaded document using an in-pipeline OpenCV detector.
> - **Grid Placement**: To harmonize "Document Photo", "Extracted Information", and "Document Validation" across 3 balanced columns, the "Alerts & Flags" card is placed with "Risk Assessment" in column 3 of row 1. This balances the height of the tall "Document Upload" card and allows the document credentials row to display all three document identity cards side-by-side.

