## Proposed Changes

### AI Service (`python_ai`)

#### [NEW] `python_ai/models/face_detection_yunet_2023mar.onnx`
- Lightweight (232 KB) OpenCV official YuNet face detector model with zero external heavy dependencies. Tested and verified in the workspace environment (detects document faces in ~20ms with >83% confidence).

#### [MODIFY] [main.py](file:///c:/Users/ritik/OneDrive/Desktop/PehchaanAI/python_ai/main.py)
- Add `extract_document_photo(image_bytes_list)` utility:
  - Runs face detection on the uploaded front document image.
  - Handles in-the-wild document orientations (tests 0°, 90°, 180°, 270° rotations to handle photos taken at any angle).
  - Adds a proportional portrait margin (~20%) around the detected facial area to present a natural portrait photo rather than a tight facial crop.
  - Computes image quality metrics:
    - Laplacian blur variance: flags blur if variance < 30.
    - Resolution and contrast check.
    - Sets quality to `'good'` ("Photo Detected") or `'low'` ("Photo Detected — Low Quality").
  - Encodes the cropped photo as standard base64 JPEG (`data:image/jpeg;base64,...`).
  - If no face is detected or image processing fails:
    ```json
    {
      "available": false,
      "image": null,
      "quality": "unavailable",
      "message": "Unable to scan or detect a clear photo from the document."
    }
    ```
  - If face is detected:
    ```json
    {
      "available": true,
      "image": "data:image/jpeg;base64,...",
      "quality": "good",
      "message": "Photo Detected"
    }
    ```
  - Attaches `photo` to the `/analyze-document` response.

#### [MODIFY] [face_api.py](file:///c:/Users/ritik/OneDrive/Desktop/PehchaanAI/python_ai/face_api.py)
- Optionally add a companion `/extract-face` endpoint to the DeepFace service on port 5001 for seamless dual-service support.

